**Theorem 4.2 (Mandatory splitting-event mass).** Suppose the normalized
certificate (4.2)–(4.3) is globally product-positive. Let

$$
\alpha_s=\sum_{J\in\{\{2\},\{5\}\}}
\operatorname{tr}(A_J^++A_J^-),\qquad
\alpha_p=\sum_{J\in\mathcal J_{\rm split}\setminus\{\{2\},\{5\}\}}
\operatorname{tr}(A_J^++A_J^-),\qquad \alpha=\alpha_s+\alpha_p.
\tag{4.6}
$$

Then

$$
\begin{aligned}
c_{\rm cert}
&\le\frac12+\frac{\sqrt{17}-3}{8}\alpha_s
+\frac{\sqrt{145}-11}{24}\alpha_p\\
&\le\frac12+\frac{\sqrt{17}-3}{8}\alpha.
\end{aligned}
\tag{4.7}
$$

In particular a value $c_{\rm cert}\ge L_*=129931/250000$ requires

$$
\alpha\ge\frac{4931(\sqrt{17}+3)}{250000}>\frac7{50}.
\tag{4.8}
$$

If $\alpha_s=0$, it requires the stronger pair-mass condition

$$
\alpha_p\ge\frac{4931(\sqrt{145}+11)}{250000}>\frac9{20}.
\tag{4.9}
$$

Proof. Express the actual thirteen-flag channel $\mathcal B$ by its
real product factors. It is invariant under $\mathcal G$, so twirling
that finite sum gives the same channel. Its full TP marginal is the
one in (4.5). Global atom positivity therefore gives

$$
c_{\rm cert}\le
\sum_J\operatorname{tr}(Z_JH_J(\mathcal B))
\le\sum_J\|H_J(\mathcal B)\|_{\rm op}
\operatorname{tr}(A_J^++A_J^-).
\tag{4.10}
$$

The last inequality follows from PSD trace pairing with both signed
Loewner bounds. Apply the simultaneous event table of Theorem 3.2:
every keep-event norm is at most $1/2$, singleton split norms are
$(1+\sqrt{17})/8$, and pair split norms are
$(1+\sqrt{145})/24$. Normalization proves (4.7).

Since $L_*-1/2=4931/250000$, rationalizing with
$(\sqrt{17}-3)(\sqrt{17}+3)=8$ proves (4.8).
The comparison $\sqrt{17}>41/10$ gives its strict rational bound.
If $\alpha_s=0$, rationalize using $145-121=24$ to obtain (4.9).
Its strict bound follows from $\sqrt{145}>12$ and
$4931\cdot23/250000>9/20$. This concerns normalized QJM-form
certificates, not every possible representation of a lower-bound
proof. It supplies no multipliers or sufficient positivity condition.
$\square$

